{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "updated": "2026-08-03",
  "notes": [
    "A catalogue of known battery pack models. When a passport identifies the pack, these values fill whatever the passport left out (chemistry, energy, mass, module count) and supply the model-specific prices the reuse and parts-out pathways need.",
    "A passport's own declarations ALWAYS win. Catalogue values are only used for fields the passport is silent about, and every filled field is recorded in the enrichment provenance.",
    "confidence expresses how well established a model's figures are: 'high' for widely documented mainstream packs, 'medium' where sources disagree on mass or module count.",
    "used_module_value_eur and oem_replacement_price_eur_per_kwh move with the used-parts market and should be refreshed from live listings. See PackDataProvider for wiring a live layer in.",
    "components: when a model omits them they are synthesised from the archetype mass split. Explicit lists are given where teardown data is well established."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "OEM service documentation and homologation filings",
    "Published pack teardowns and dismantling manuals",
    "Used-parts marketplace listings for the module and BMS value ranges"
  ],
